LAYOUTS

Compact keyboard layout definitions and compose rules for tam-last,
compiled at build time into C tables by tools/gen-layouts.c.

FORMAT (.layout)

  UTF-8 text, one entry per line. Lines whose first non-space byte is
  '#' are comments.

  Directives:
    name <id>           layout identifier (for --layout and tam-last.ini)
    altgr none|rightalt whether KEY_RIGHTALT acts as AltGr (level 3/4)
    include <id>        copy base mappings from an earlier layout

  Key lines:
    KEY_<NAME>  <lvl0>  <lvl1>  [<lvl2>  [<lvl3>]]

    lvl0 = base, lvl1 = Shift, lvl2 = AltGr, lvl3 = AltGr+Shift.
    Omitted lvl2/lvl3 default to none.

  Tokens:
    none                unmapped level (0)
    space               U+0020
    U+XXXX              Unicode codepoint (4-6 hex digits)
    dead_<name>         dead key (dead_acute, dead_grave,
                        dead_circumflex, dead_tilde, dead_diaeresis,
                        dead_cedilla, dead_ring)
    <char>              any single UTF-8 character

FORMAT (compose)

  One rule per line:
    <sym1> <sym2> [<sym3> [<sym4>]] -> <result>

  Dead-key rules begin with dead_<name>. Multi-key Compose sequences
  begin with the token 'compose' (triggered by KEY_COMPOSE). No rule
  may be a prefix of another; gen-layouts rejects conflicts at build
  time.
